        "id": 221496,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-01T02:49:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, what MindWanderer said. It only mattered in some edge cases, and so at the table we just used the tie = players’ choice principle.</p>\n<p>I know that’s not the official rule, and I know that’s not how it happens in the video game, but like I said, it rarely mattered very much.</p>\n<p>Anyway, I’m over it; Benchmark is an interesting mechanism to play with and a discard-fueled character doesn’t suffer for having an Enduring Intercession in her deck.</p>",
